<p>
	<label for="settings_hangouts_chat_url">Google Chat URL</label>
	<input type="text" id="settings_hangouts_chat_url" size=80 value="<%= settings['hangouts_chat_url'] %>" name="settings[hangouts_chat_url]" />
</p>

<p>
	Generate a webhook URL for target the channel. This URL can be changed on a per-project basis by creating a <a href="/custom_fields/new?type=ProjectCustomField">project custom field</a> named "Google Chat URL" (without quotes).
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_thread">Google Chat Thread</label>
	<input type="text" id="settings_thread" value="<%= settings['thread'] %>" name="settings[thread]" />
</p>

<p>
	The messages can be threaded a per-project basis by creating a
	<a href="/custom_fields/new?type=ProjectCustomField">project custom field</a> named "Google Chat Thread" (without quotes).
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_thread_per_issue">One Thread per Issue?</label>
	<input type="checkbox" id="settings_thread_per_issue" value="1" name="settings[thread_per_issue]" <%= settings['thread_per_issue'] == '1' ? 'checked="checked"' : '' %> />
</p>

<p>
	Posts all messages about an issue to a thread of its own named "&lt;thread&gt;-issue-&lt;id&gt;" instead of the project thread.
	Without a thread, it is named "redmine-issue-&lt;id&gt;"; a project thread "-" still disables the messages. Wiki updates stay in the project thread.
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_username">Google Chat Username</label>
	<input type="text" id="settings_username" value="<%= settings['username'] %>" name="settings[username]" />
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_display_watchers">Display Watchers?</label>
	<select id="settings_display_watchers" value="<%= settings['display_watchers'] %>" name="settings[display_watchers]">
		<option value="yes">Yes</option>
		<option value="no" <%= settings['display_watchers'] != 'yes' ? %q(selected="selected") : '' %>>No</option>
	</select>
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_post_updates">Post Issue Updates?</label>
	<input type="checkbox" id="settings_post_updates" value="1" name="settings[post_updates]" <%= settings['post_updates'] == '1' ? 'checked="checked"' : '' %> />
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_post_wiki_updates">Post Wiki Updates?</label>
	<input type="checkbox" id="settings_post_wiki_updates" value="1" name="settings[post_wiki_updates]" <%= settings['post_wiki_updates'] == '1' ? 'checked="checked"' : '' %> />
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_ignored_fields">Ignored Fields</label>
	<textarea id="settings_ignored_fields" rows="4" cols="40" name="settings[ignored_fields]"><%= settings['ignored_fields'] %></textarea>
</p>

<p>
	Changes to these fields are not posted, one field per line. Use the name of a custom field or of an issue attribute. Updates which only change ignored fields and have no notes are not sent at all.
</p>
